    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.93"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The rule is exact, inexpensive to run, and the distinction between boundary and interior can be measured directly. Existing computation can confirm complex finite boundary dynamics, which is sufficient for the existential core." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Reproduce the exactly specified growth rule, track boundary shape descriptors over time, and compare predictability, periodicity, symmetry, and compressibility against simple-shape growth controls. Persistent irregular boundary dynamics confirms that complexity occurs in overall shape." ;
